      "The \"reducing balance\" part matters more than the formula itself. Each month, your instalment is split into an interest portion and a principal portion. Interest is charged only on the principal you still owe - not on the original loan amount. Because the outstanding principal shrinks every month, the interest portion of each EMI shrinks too, while the principal portion grows. Your EMI amount stays fixed for the whole tenure; only the split changes.",
