      "## 5. Frequently Asked Questions on Percentage Conversions",
      "### Should internal assessment / project marks be separated from final exam marks?\nUnless an application specifically requests separate theory and practical breakdowns, sum both components into a single subject total before calculating aggregate percentages.\n\n### How should decimal percentages be rounded off?\nNever round up unless instructed. A score of 59.94% is not 60.00%. If an engineering cutoff is strictly 60.00%, entering 60.0% constitutes misrepresentation and leads to immediate disqualification.\n\n### How do foreign universities treat Indian percentage marks?\nInternational credential evaluators (like WES) recompute raw marks using proprietary credit-weighting algorithms rather than applying flat multipliers.",
